                new ("003Qx00000f3jSYIAY", new UNOPSContact
                {
                    Name = "Takao Asamura",
                    ContactNumber = "003Qx00000f3jSYIAY",
                    Salutation = "Mr.",
                    FirstName = "Takao",
                    MiddleName = null,
                    LastName = "Asamura",
                    Suffix = "Ph.D",
                    Title = "Contact",
                    Department = "Embassy of Japan to Ukraine",
                    Description = "Dear Elene, Thank you for your mail and for hosting us this week in your premises. And thank you indeed for this thorough information you share with us in your email. Have a nice weekend and receive our warm wishes, Patricio   Patricio Rumeu Casares Consejero/Counselor Embajada de España en Ucrania / Embassy of Spain to Ukraine Khoryva 46 - 04071 Kyiv + 38 044 5210732 e-mail: patricio.rumeu@maec.es   www.exteriores.gob.es                  From: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org> Sent: Friday, April 4, 2025 4:24:51 PM To: pablo.gan@aecid.es <pablo.gan@aecid.es>; Rumeu Casares, Patricio <patricio.rumeu@maec.es> Cc: Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org> Subject: Follow-up: Energy/Heating Needs Project in Ukraine   Dear Ambassador Quesada, Dear Patricio, Following up on our conversation, I wanted to provide an update regarding the potential project to address energy/heating needs in Ukraine. As requested, we've gathered updated information on the district heating sector's priorities and critical needs, as identified by WASH partners. Attached, you'll find overviews of the district heating needs in: Izium, Kharkiv oblast Balakliya, Kharkiv oblast Chernihiv Shostka Poltava We also have information from authorities in the Vinnytsia region, primarily covering modular boiler houses, which we can provide if that location is preferred. Based on this information, we would like to discuss your preferred location for the project. We suggest focusing on the procurement of: Cogeneration units Modular boiler houses Pumps, pipes, valves, and other supportive materials To give you an idea of costs, a 250-260 kW cogeneration unit is estimated at around USD 350,000, while a 5 MW modular boiler house is around USD 800,000-850,000. Supportive materials would be lower in cost. With your prioritization, we can design a procurement project with an estimated duration of 11 months. Of course, we will coordinate with other partners to avoid duplication. If this approach is acceptable, we will prepare a detailed concept note/project proposal. For you reference, we have also made initial high-level budget estimations for a project under USD 2 million: Engagement Budget Categories\tTotal in USD Activities/Procurement\t$1,400,000 Personnel\t$302,193 Non-personnel\t$145,193 UNOPS Fee\t$144,224 TOTAL\t$1,991,611 Please let us know your thoughts and we'd be happy to discuss this in more detail on a call. With thanks and kind regards Elene On Tue, Apr 1, 2025 at 4:30 PM Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org> wrote: Dear Ambassador Quesada, Dear Patricio, Many thanks for the meeting earlier today and for your interest in exploring partnership with UNOPS to support emergency needs in Ukraine. Let me share with you some background materials about UNOPS procurement rules and our partnership with the EU. We appreciate your interest in strengthening the water and energy systems and we will revert soon with some options. We look very much forward to working with you and please don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions on UNOPS operations in Ukraine or in general. Kind regards, Elene  Elene Agladze |Partnerships Specialist | Ukraine Multi-Country Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel: +380 956 00 1880 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
